# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# The repo is ~291 GB, overwhelmingly `market_data/` (280 GB of parquet and
# csv). Docker tars the whole build context before it sends a byte to the
# daemon, so without this the build spends minutes transferring data the image
# never uses -- the measured transfer rate on this repo was ~15 MB/s against a
# 3.5 GB context, and the context was 3.5 GB only because the previous run's
# cache had already trimmed it.
#
# Everything here is either (a) data, (b) a build artifact, or (c) tooling that
# exists on the host. The container rebuilds (b) from source and reaches (a)
# and (c) through the compose bind mounts, not through the image.
# =============================================================================

# --- Market data: the single biggest item, 280 GB ---------------------------
# Bind-mounted read/write in docker-compose.dev.yml instead.
market_data/

# --- Python virtualenv: 6 GB, and the container has its own interpreter -----
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Rust build artifacts: rebuilt inside the image from source -------------
# Not just noise -- shipping a Windows-built target/ into a Linux image is
# actively wrong, since the artifacts are not portable.
target/
**/target/

# --- Python caches ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Git history: 1.4 GB, and nothing in the build reads it ----------------
.git/
.github/

# --- Secrets: never bake a key into a layer --------------------------------
.env
*.key
*.pem

# --- Editor / OS noise ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- Local output artifacts ------------------------------------------------
out/
build/
*.log

# --- Prebuilt wheels: the root Dockerfile consumes these, the dev image
# does not. Present in the context they would be copied in by `COPY . .`.
dist/

# --- Docs are not needed to build or run -----------------------------------
docs/
*.md
